That's not really true. Why would you need a getBar() method in Java?<p><pre><code>    public class Foo
      int bar;

      public Foo(int initBar) {
        bar = initBar;
      }

      public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(new Foo(42).bar);
      }
    }</code></pre>
